```text
==============================================================
=/                   V P O R T  P R O T O                   \=
==============================================================

      Wire protocol definitions for the VPort protocol


  VPort is a tiny display protocol for embedded and
  point-of-sale Linux systems. A client talks to a display
  server and the server draws in an isolated portal.

  VPort proto holds the reference wire definitions in Rust:
  the frame header, the opcodes, the messages, and their
  encoding and decoding. It has no dependencies.

  STATUS: early release. The protocol is a draft and can
  change in any 0.x version.

  The specification and the reference programs (the vportd
  server, the vport-gateway and the libvport client library)
  are in the VPort repository linked from this crate.


--[ EXAMPLE ]-------------------------------------------------

  use vport_proto::{Commit, Message};

  let mut bytes = Vec::new();
  Message::Commit(Commit { portal_id: 1 }).encode_into(&mut bytes);


==============================================================
```
